Add the @diced tomatoes{14%oz}(undrained), @garlic{6%cloves}(minced), @ginger{1%tbsp}(minced), @ground turmeric{1%tsp}, @ground cayenne pepper{1%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @garam masala{2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, and @salt{1%tsp} in the #Instant Pot{}. Stir thoroughly and nestle the @chicken breast{1%lb}(boneless skinless, or thighs) in.

Put the lid on and set the pressure to high for ~{10%minutes}. Let the pressure release naturally for ~{10%minutes}, then depressurize.

Carefully open the lid and remove the chicken. Use an immersion blender and blend the sauce until smooth. Alternately, carefully transfer to a blender and blend until smooth. Let cool slightly for ~{3-5%minutes} then stir in the @butter{1/2%cubed}, @heavy cream{1/2%cup}, and the last teaspoon of @garam masala{}. The sauce should be thick enough to coat the back of a spoon.

Roughly chop the chicken then add back into the sauce. Set the Instant Pot to sauté on low, letting the chicken heat through. Top with the @fresh cilantro{1/2%cup}(chopped) and enjoy with basmati and naan!
